      "description": "Watch Malaga vs Deportivo La Coruna highlights and goals from La Liga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 24, 2026. Hard-Fought Stalemate in La Liga On August 24, 2026, the football world turned its attention to a clash between Malaga and Deportivo de La Coruna , where two determined sides fought for dominance on the pitch. The tactical battle remained tight throughout, with neither side able to pull away despite moments of individual brilliance. First Half Momentum Deportivo de La Coruna struck first, with Pierre-Emerick Aubameyang finding the net in the 21st minute following a clever assist from Luismi Cruz . This early goal forced Malaga to push forward in search of an equalizer. Their persistence paid off in the 34th minute when Rafita was brought down in the box by Lucas Noubi . Chupe stepped up to the spot, firing home a precise penalty with his right foot that barely eluded Leo Roman 's reach, bringing the scoreline level. Tactical Struggles and Intensity As the second half progressed, the game became increasingly physical, characterized by a series of yellow cards for Giacomo Quagliata , David Larrubia , Mario Soriano , and Ximo Navarro . Both managers looked to their benches to inject fresh energy, introducing players like Yeremay Hernandez , David Mella , and Ramon Enriquez . Despite a flurry of late-game efforts from the hosts to find a winning goal, the defensive units held firm, ensuring the points were shared as the referee blew the final whistle."
